From 369e0a3334a4c682fa679c9583c98be0ec4e9b30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew <matthewhale@live.com.au>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 22:04:13 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 34/59] Threat display boarding time, XvT engine wash

- Threat display (Z): while the target is docked and boarding (or is the
  craft being boarded), "BOARDING TIME LEFT" counts down in place of the
  travel time. On the way in, the full boarding time follows the travel
  time ("+ 2:00 BOARDING"). paiman_boardmaneuver runs aiOrderProgress
  units of 14160 ticks (one mission minute) once docked.
- game.xvt_engine_wash (OpenXvT collide_ApplyEngineWashDamage): every 29
  mission ticks, the player behind a working freighter's or starship's
  OPT engine meshes (component 6) takes up to 64 damage per engine, on
  the shield bank facing the engine; 1/8 with shields down. Front-half
  engines (CAL.OPT bow pods) are skipped. Clocked from the mission clock
  so replays repeat it. XvT's warning message, at most every 5 s.
